          "timestamp": "2026-10-15T00:18:39Z",
          "diff_summary": "#2199/#2216, Owner fallback to option B (2026-10-15). ENFORCEMENT MODE: RECORD-ONLY. The canonical research path RECORDS a contamination signal and does NOT block; the research auto-flow does not change research_gate_passed and does not quarantine the research context. Upgrading to blocking is a later Owner decision, based on the accumulated signals. Code commit 8e1da0e9b is a PR-branch commit (pre squash-merge). ROUTES: (1) canonical research executor nexus/core/capability_executor_registry.py _exec_research -> _research_contamination_signal: on accepted research output, the receipt keeps its normal status and its outcome carries contamination_signal {policy_id, mode: record_only, detected: true|false, reason: RESEARCH_CONTAMINATION_DETECTED|'', terms}; when the check cannot run, detected=null and reason=RESEARCH_CONTAMINATION_GUARD_ERROR. (2) research auto-flow nexus/app/research_flow_service.py run_auto_flow -> record_flow_contamination_signal: the same signal goes into capability_evidence and nexus_usage_trace.capabilities.research_contamination_signal. Both routes append every signal to <workspace>/.nexus/research/contamination_signals.jsonl (schema nexus.research.contamination_signal.v1) for later aggregation. WHAT IS SCANNED: strings, dict keys (as text), lists/tuples/sets, bytes, dataclasses, pydantic models and plain objects (vars); design-field names at any depth; other object types, or more than 200000 nodes / depth 64, give GUARD_ERROR. For the auto-flow the planner-owned context keys (FLOW_CONTEXT_PLANNER_KEYS) are not scanned. DETECTION: CANONICAL_DESIGN_PATTERNS, structural regexes (modal + design verb, 'the fix/plan/solution is to', labelled prefixes, 'can be fixed by', we recommend/propose, diff hunks, Chinese equivalents) on NFKC/zero-width/hyphen-normalised text; a match is discounted only when fully inside a clean task/query echo. MEASURED: held-out (coordinator corpus, unseen by the author) detection 53/120 (44%), Chinese 18/40; held-out clean-text false positives 4/120 (3.3%, quoted-doc recommendations). Below the 70% detection bar for blocking, hence record-only. Author measurements 2026-10-15: proxy false positives Nexus-new issue title+body 20/500 (4.0%), docs 300-word chunks 97/2661 (3.6%), historical research packs 0/59; reviewer dev set 37/38 (tuned on it); own untuned fresh sets 17/40 and 17/40 (42%). ALSO IN THIS CHANGE: build_research_facts keeps findings when blocked_assumptions is present. NOT COVERED: (a) design advice phrased outside the patterns (held-out recall 44%); bare code blocks with a suggested change. (b) the legacy pipeline_stages research stage (facts_only and L0) and the phase_factory/phase_executors research phase are not wired; they are not in the static import closure of the live entrypoints (nexus CLI, MCP gateway and server modules), pinned by test_legacy_research_routes_unreachable_from_live_entrypoints; dynamic (string/port) imports are outside that proof. (c) the canonical executor still sends the unmasked task to the provider; this is an output signal, not L1/L2 isolation. Real rollback drill: addendum 4 in docs/reports/contamination-guard-rollback-drill-2026-10-14.md.",
